            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0584" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/906: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sterling</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-24T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>37. Your no. 36, dated April 21, 1 p.m. The Department feels that it is extremely
                    unfortunate that so long a delay has occurred, as it may prejudice the success
                    of the conference at the outset. If the conference should not begin before May
                    15, the Chilean delegates will have been kept waiting for nearly one month.</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that Ambassador Pezet arrives May 8, the Department believes
                    that May 10 could be the date of the formal opening of the conference. Convey
                    the foregoing informally to the Government of Peru, and inquire as to whether
                    this date is agreeable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
